What changed in this fork
-------------------------

* Name, application id (dev.sifluxlab.dshnext), deep-link scheme (dshnext://),
  launcher labels and documentation were rebranded to DSH NEXT.
* 酒馆 (Tavern), 创意工坊 (Workshop) and 伙伴小屋 (Companion) became optional
  built-in plugins: 设置 › 内置插件 switches each one on or off at runtime.
* The upstream author's services are no longer contacted. Every host that used
  to point at them (updates mirror, relay, forum, workshop, plugin market,
  usage reporting, hosted shares) now points at the reserved placeholder
  dshnext.invalid, which never resolves. Configure your own deployment there
  (see docs/dsh-next.md) or leave the features off.
* Brand artwork, mascots and the Live2D material are not part of this tree.
  Assets owned by the upstream author were removed; see ASSETS.md upstream for
  what was never covered by the AGPL.

Upstream files that are intentionally unchanged
-----------------------------------------------

Internal identifiers that the engine patch set, the runtime layout and the
plugin protocol depend on keep their upstream names (for example
runtime/bridge/dsh-go-bridge, /opt/dsh-go inside the guest, the
dsh-go-companion-full preset, and the dshGo service name). Renaming them would
break the patched engine and every already-published plugin; they are not
user-visible.

Third-party components, fonts, icons and runtime pieces keep their own licences
(THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
